accessWidener   v1  official

# 26.3 moved a Biome's MobSpawnSettings into its EnvironmentAttributeMap (as the
# gameplay/natural_mob_spawns EnvironmentAttribute), so BiomeModification no longer mutates
# MobSpawnSettings.spawners (which 26.3 also renamed to spawnsByCategory) in place - see MobSettingsWorker
# for why doing so would now be unsafe. It instead replaces the built Biome's attribute map with a derived
# one, which needs this otherwise private final field to be writable.
accessible field net/minecraft/world/level/biome/Biome attributes Lnet/minecraft/world/attribute/EnvironmentAttributeMap;
mutable field net/minecraft/world/level/biome/Biome attributes Lnet/minecraft/world/attribute/EnvironmentAttributeMap;
